# 5. PHASE 3: PRIVACY AND DOCUMENT SECURITY

This is a critical phase.

## 5.1 Backup configuration

The current manifest enables:

`android:allowBackup="true"`

The current backup rule files contain sample or incomplete configuration.

Inspect the actual storage implementation and classify every data location:

- Private documents.
- Original scans.
- Exported PDFs.
- Temporary files.
- Signatures.
- OCR text.
- Database files.
- User preferences.
- Cache and thumbnails.

Define the backup policy explicitly.

Default product requirement:

- Private document vault must not enter cloud backup.
- Temporary files must not enter backup.
- Sensitive signatures must not enter cloud backup.
- Document databases containing sensitive content must not be backed up without explicit product approval.
- Preferences can be backed up only if they do not contain sensitive information.
- Device-to-device transfer behavior must be documented separately.

Implement the appropriate Android backup and data extraction rules for supported Android versions.

Verify behavior on API 30 and API 31+.

Do not assume that an empty backup rule file excludes everything.

## 5.2 App-private vault

Verify:

- Files are stored in the correct app-private location.
- No unnecessary external storage permission is requested.
- File names are safely handled.
- Temporary files are removed only when safe.
- Exported files are not accidentally deleted.
- FileProvider exposes only required paths.
- URI permissions are granted only to intended recipients.
- Imported files are validated before processing.
- Malformed documents cannot crash the application.

If encryption is implemented or proposed, use Android Keystore-backed key management and established cryptographic libraries. Do not invent custom encryption.

Never claim that the vault is encrypted unless encryption is actually implemented and tested.

## 5.3 Camera and file permissions

Keep permissions minimal.

Camera permission should be requested only when the scanner is opened.

Use:

- Android Photo Picker for image selection.
- Storage Access Framework for document selection and export.
- Temporary URI grants where appropriate.

Handle:

- Permission denied.
- Permission permanently denied.
- Camera unavailable.
- Camera hardware unavailable.
- Selected file no longer accessible.
- URI permission revoked.
- Insufficient storage.

## 5.4 Data deletion

Implement reliable deletion behavior.

When the user deletes a document:

- Remove its database record.
- Remove associated stored files.
- Remove related thumbnails and temporary derivatives.
- Handle deletion failures without leaving misleading UI.
- Protect against deleting files outside the app-owned directory.

Provide a confirmation for destructive batch operations.

